{"format": 2, "style": {"font": "EB Garamond", "noteSize": 12}, "meta": {"title": "Service of the Word", "sunday": "An Example Sunday", "date": "January 1, 2027"}, "cover": {"show": true, "image": "img:emblem", "footer": ["Example Church", "Anytown"]}, "parts": [{"name": "Welcome page", "side": false, "size": 13, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "html": "<b>Welcome to Example Church</b>", "float": "img:emblem", "floatSide": "left", "floatWidth": "15%"}, {"type": "text", "html": "This is an example bulletin that comes with Grammateus. Open it, change the words, and save it under a new name to make your own. Nothing here is specific to any one church."}, {"type": "text", "html": "<b>How to read this bulletin</b>", "align": "center"}, {"type": "text", "html": "An asterisk (*) before a heading invites you to stand, as you are able. <b>Bold print</b> is said by everyone together. <i>Italic print</i> gives directions. The grey column explains parts of the service."}, {"type": "text", "html": "<b>How this bulletin is put together</b>", "align": "center"}, {"type": "text", "html": "It is made of parts: this welcome page, the service, extra pages and the back page. Every part can hold any kind of item, and each part chooses whether its pages have the grey side column for notes."}]}, {"name": "The service", "side": true, "size": 15, "blocks": [{"type": "section", "text": "Gathering"}, {"type": "heading", "text": "Prelude", "stand": false}, {"type": "heading", "text": "Greeting", "stand": true, "note": "The greeting is among the oldest parts of Christian worship."}, {"type": "text", "html": "The Lord be with you.<br><b>And also with you.</b>"}, {"type": "heading", "text": "Gathering Hymn", "stand": true}, {"type": "hymn", "title": "Amazing Grace", "number": "No. 1", "note": "<u>Hymn Information</u><br>Text: John Newton, 1725–1807<br>Music: an example only"}, {"type": "image", "src": "img:music1"}, {"type": "heading", "text": "Prayer of the Day", "stand": true, "note": "This prayer gathers the themes of the day's readings."}, {"type": "text", "html": "Let us pray.<br>Gracious God, be present with your people gathered here, that we may hear your word and be glad.<br><b>Amen.</b>"}, {"type": "section", "text": "Word"}, {"type": "heading", "text": "First Reading", "stand": false, "ref": "Jeremiah 31:31–34", "note": "The first reading is usually from the Old Testament. All the readings here are from the World English Bible, which is in the public domain."}, {"type": "text", "html": "<sup>31</sup>“Behold, the days come,” says the <span class=\"sc\">Lord</span>, “that I will make a new covenant with the house of Israel, and with the house of Judah, <sup>32</sup>not according to the covenant that I made with their fathers in the day that I took them by the hand to bring them out of the land of Egypt, which covenant of mine they broke, although I was a husband to them,” says the <span class=\"sc\">Lord</span>."}, {"type": "text", "html": "<sup>33</sup>“But this is the covenant that I will make with the house of Israel after those days,” says the <span class=\"sc\">Lord</span>: “I will put my law in their inward parts, and I will write it in their heart. I will be their God, and they shall be my people. <sup>34</sup>They will no longer each teach his neighbor, and every man teach his brother, saying, ‘Know the <span class=\"sc\">Lord</span>;’ for they will all know me, from their least to their greatest,” says the <span class=\"sc\">Lord</span>, “for I will forgive their iniquity, and I will remember their sin no more.”"}, {"type": "text", "html": "The word of the Lord.<br><b>Thanks be to God.</b>"}, {"type": "heading", "text": "Psalm", "stand": false, "ref": "Psalm 40:6–10", "note": "The psalm is often sung or read together, as a response to the first reading."}, {"type": "text", "html": "<sup>6</sup>Sacrifice and offering you didn’t desire.<br>You have opened my ears.<br>You have not required burnt offering and sin offering.<br><sup>7</sup>Then I said, “Behold, I have come.<br>It is written about me in the book in the scroll.<br><sup>8</sup>I delight to do your will, my God.<br>Yes, your law is within my heart.”"}, {"type": "text", "html": "<sup>9</sup>I have proclaimed glad news of righteousness in the great assembly.<br>Behold, I will not seal my lips, <span class=\"sc\">Lord</span>, you know.<br><sup>10</sup>I have not hidden your righteousness within my heart.<br>I have declared your faithfulness and your salvation.<br>I have not concealed your loving kindness and your truth from the great assembly."}, {"type": "heading", "text": "Second Reading", "stand": false, "ref": "2 Corinthians 3:1–6", "note": "The second reading is usually from one of the letters in the New Testament."}, {"type": "text", "html": "<sup>1</sup>Are we beginning again to commend ourselves? Or do we need, as do some, letters of commendation to you or from you? <sup>2</sup>You are our letter, written in our hearts, known and read by all men, <sup>3</sup>being revealed that you are a letter of Christ, served by us, written not with ink, but with the Spirit of the living God; not in tablets of stone, but in tablets that are hearts of flesh."}, {"type": "text", "html": "<sup>4</sup>Such confidence we have through Christ toward God, <sup>5</sup>not that we are sufficient of ourselves to account anything as from ourselves; but our sufficiency is from God, <sup>6</sup>who also made us sufficient as servants of a new covenant, not of the letter but of the Spirit. For the letter kills, but the Spirit gives life."}, {"type": "text", "html": "The word of the Lord.<br><b>Thanks be to God.</b>"}, {"type": "heading", "text": "Gospel", "stand": true, "ref": "Luke 24:28–32", "note": "The assembly stands to hear the Gospel."}, {"type": "text", "html": "<sup>28</sup>They came near to the village where they were going, and he acted like he would go further. <sup>29</sup>They urged him, saying, “Stay with us, for it is almost evening, and the day is almost over.” He went in to stay with them. <sup>30</sup>When he had sat down at the table with them, he took the bread and gave thanks. Breaking it, he gave it to them. <sup>31</sup>Their eyes were opened and they recognized him; then he vanished out of their sight. <sup>32</sup>They said to one another, “Weren’t our hearts burning within us while he spoke to us along the way, and while he opened the Scriptures to us?”"}, {"type": "text", "html": "The Gospel of the Lord.<br><b>Praise to you, O Christ.</b>"}, {"type": "heading", "text": "Sermon", "stand": false}, {"type": "text", "html": "<i>A time of silence follows the sermon.</i>"}, {"type": "heading", "text": "Hymn of the Day", "stand": true}, {"type": "hymn", "title": "A Longer Example Hymn", "number": "No. 2"}, {"type": "image", "src": "img:music2"}, {"type": "heading", "text": "Prayers", "stand": true, "note": "We pray for the church, the world, and all who are in need."}, {"type": "text", "html": "<i>After each petition:</i><br>Lord, in your mercy,<br><b>hear our prayer.</b>"}, {"type": "section", "text": "Sending"}, {"type": "heading", "text": "Blessing", "stand": true}, {"type": "text", "html": "The Lord bless you and keep you.<br><b>Amen.</b>"}, {"type": "heading", "text": "Dismissal", "stand": true}, {"type": "text", "html": "Go in peace.<br><b>Thanks be to God.</b>"}, {"type": "heading", "text": "Postlude", "stand": false}]}, {"name": "Extra pages", "side": false, "size": 14.5, "blocks": [{"type": "roster", "title": "Serving Today", "rows": [{"left": "Presiding", "right": "The Rev. A. N. Example"}, {"left": "Reader", "right": "A Reader"}, {"left": "Musician", "right": "A Musician"}, {"left": "Usher", "right": "An Usher"}]}, {"type": "heading", "text": "Announcements", "stand": false}, {"type": "rule"}, {"type": "text", "html": "<b>Coffee hour</b><br>Coffee hour follows the service. All are welcome."}, {"type": "rule"}, {"type": "text", "html": "<b>About these pages</b><br>Pages like this one use the full width of the page. Add or remove whole sheets of paper with the buttons at the top of the window."}]}, {"name": "Back page", "side": false, "size": 14, "last": true, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "html": "<b>You are welcome here.</b>", "align": "center"}, {"type": "text", "html": "Example Church · 1 Example Street · Anytown", "align": "center"}, {"type": "logos", "images": ["img:emblem"]}]}], "extraSheets": 0, "images": {"emblem": "data:image/png;base64,", "music1": "data:image/png;base64,", "music2": "data:image/png;base64,"}}